# vehje-runtime-zig. Design

Zig implementation of the vehje runtime. Consumes the C ABI
(vehje-runtime-abi); implements the entry points with a Vehje-
IR interpreter, scratch-var folding, and generative expansion.

## Scope

- Arena allocator. per-session state owning compile-time
  buffers.
- IR interpreter. evaluates macro bodies + generative subgraph
  blueprints against the incoming ABI node buffers.
- Scratch-var evaluator. folds compile-time expressions to byte
  blobs the compiler re-inserts into the AST.
- TokenStream emitter. macros return AbiToken arrays.
- Error reporter. maps Zig-side failures to AbiDiagnostic.

## Round-skeleton scope

Phase 6 skeleton round (2026-04-20) ships:

- `build.zig` declaring a `clause_runtime` shared-library
  target. Output: `zig-out/lib/libclause_runtime.{so|dylib|dll}`.
- `src/runtime.zig` exporting three `extern "C"` stubs matching
  the Rust `vehje-runtime-abi` exports:
  - `clause_runtime_new() ?*anyopaque` → null.
  - `clause_runtime_free(?*anyopaque) void` → no-op.
  - `clause_runtime_execute(?*anyopaque, [*]const u8, usize) i32`
    → `CLAUSE_RESULT_ERR` (`-1`).
  - `pub const CLAUSE_RESULT_OK: i32 = 0;` (+ `_ERR`,
    `_NULL_HANDLE`, `_INVALID_INPUT` matching the Rust
    discriminants).
- `README.md` describing the tree + build workflow.
- `.gitignore` excluding `zig-out/`, `zig-cache/`.
- `BACKLOG.md` listing deferred runtime features.

### `ClauseResult` ABI layout. scalar i32

The Rust side declares `#[repr(i32)] enum ClauseResult { Ok = 0,
Err = -1, NullHandle = -2, InvalidInput = -3 }`. On System V
x86-64 and Apple ARM64 this lowers to a scalar-in-register
return. The Zig side returns plain `i32` directly, giving
identical register-use on every target.

Alternative considered and rejected: mirror the Rust enum via
`pub const ClauseResult = extern struct { code: i32 }` (a
one-field wrapper struct). Rejected because on MSVC Windows
x64 a one-field extern struct returns via hidden-pointer
(sret) while a `#[repr(i32)]` enum returns in `eax`. the two
sides would disagree on the calling convention. Scalar `i32`
return is the trivially portable form across every ABI.

Named constants (`CLAUSE_RESULT_OK`, `CLAUSE_RESULT_ERR`,
`CLAUSE_RESULT_NULL_HANDLE`, `CLAUSE_RESULT_INVALID_INPUT`)
mirror the Rust discriminants exactly and give Zig-side call
sites a readable form instead of bare integer literals.

Real interpreter body, arena allocator, scratch-var evaluator,
TokenStream emitter, and Zig test suite are all BACKLOG.

## Non-scope

- The ABI contract itself (`vehje-runtime-abi`).
- The compiler-side dispatch (`vehje-runtime-driver`).
- Runtime performance tuning (post-Phase 6).

## Build integration

- `build.zig` drives the Zig compilation.
- Output: `zig-out/lib/libclause_runtime.{so|dylib|dll}`.
- Target-triple-specific builds; a distribution bundle pairs the
  Rust compiler binary with the matching dylib for each supported
  platform.
- Mockspace does not build this tree. it ships source but
  cargo / mockspace lints ignore the `.zig` files. The Zig side
  is validated only by running `zig build` manually or in CI.

## Dependencies

- Standard Zig library only. No third-party Zig packages. No
  runtime allocator. arena-only.

